attack-surface-management is the vendor-neutral external attack surface management (EASM / ASM) DESIGN
umbrella: how internet-facing assets are discovered from the attacker's outside-in perspective, how to
attribute a discovery to the organisation without drowning in false positives, the EASM-to-VM feedback
loop, attack surface reduction, and which EASM platform earns the deployment. It is the sibling to
vulnerability-management (the split decided with the user at plan time, 2026-06-18): this umbrella owns
DISCOVERY + ATTRIBUTION + EXPOSURE-REDUCTION; vulnerability-management owns the scanning and remediation of
the known assets EASM surfaces. Skill licensed MIT (the primary-source licence).

Scope + cadence (decided with the user at plan time, 2026-06-18 AskUserQuestion):
  - Split umbrellas: vulnerability-management + attack-surface-management (this skill), shipped together in
    PR 1 of the VulnMgmt + ASM family (the design layer).
  - Microsoft Defender EASM re-authored as a vault vendor skill in PR 2; Xpanse, Falcon Surface, Censys,
    Shodan named here as routing context only.
  - This umbrella owns DESIGN / DISCOVERY-METHOD / ATTRIBUTION / PLATFORM-COMPARISON only; per-platform
    operations are routed out via "When not to use".

